1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,000
Is this just all part of a deal that's been done with Hamas?

2
00:00:03,680 --> 00:00:09,100
They released Thai citizens and the hostages have to all say they were treated well.

3
00:00:09,600 --> 00:00:13,600
When we negotiated with Hamas, they didn't give any requests or conditions for release.

4
00:00:14,020 --> 00:00:17,560
They just said that the Thai hostages would be freed when there's a ceasefire.

5
00:00:18,280 --> 00:00:23,900
But Hamas did kill at least 39 Thai citizens.

6
00:00:24,420 --> 00:00:26,700
39 Thais were killed, that's for sure.

7
00:00:26,700 --> 00:00:28,820
But we don't know where or how.

8
00:00:28,820 --> 00:00:29,860
It's a war.

9
00:00:30,660 --> 00:00:36,180
It is indisputable that families were murdered by Hamas on October 7th.

10
00:00:36,520 --> 00:00:41,280
Why did you feel so sure that they would protect hostages?

11
00:00:41,700 --> 00:00:43,160
Definitely, it is a war.

12
00:00:43,920 --> 00:00:45,340
There was killing on both sides.

13
00:00:45,580 --> 00:00:48,580
But the main point of Hamas going there was to capture hostages

14
00:00:48,580 --> 00:00:51,360
and to use them for deals to help the Palestinians.

15
00:00:51,840 --> 00:00:58,500
Just to be clear, you're not denying that Hamas killed Israeli civilians, are you?

16
00:00:58,500 --> 00:01:02,900
According to Hamas, they only wanted to kill Israeli soldiers, not civilians.

17
00:01:03,360 --> 00:01:06,920
Are you sympathetic with Hamas's cause?

18
00:01:07,020 --> 00:01:11,700
And do you think that's in part why you've been able to negotiate the release of Thai citizens?

19
00:01:12,100 --> 00:01:14,300
I sympathize with the Palestinian people.

20
00:01:14,840 --> 00:01:20,800
After more and more wars, the land was taken and eventually Palestinians were refugees and made second-class citizens.

21
00:01:20,800 --> 00:01:24,180
You don't have to be a Muslim to have sympathy for Palestinians.

22
00:01:24,880 --> 00:01:29,900
Do you think that Hamas was justified in taking hostages from Israel?

23
00:01:30,320 --> 00:01:35,460
Yes, because there are more than 6,000 Palestinians captured in the past and their families can't visit them.

24
00:01:36,120 --> 00:01:37,240
No one heard their cries.

25
00:01:37,800 --> 00:01:39,280
The world didn't hear their cries.

26
00:01:39,840 --> 00:01:44,900
That's why Hamas had to do this, to get the world's attention focused on Israel's treatment of the Palestinians.

27
00:01:44,900 --> 00:01:49,420
They want to negotiate more and achieve change to get help for the people of Gaza.

